# Build context hygiene. Without this the whole workspace (node_modules, build
# output, Git history, local env files) is sent to the daemon and can leak into
# an image layer.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
**/.turbo

.git
.gitignore

# Local environment files must never be baked into an image. `apps/api/.env`
# was previously copied into the image, where pydantic-settings read it as the
# database/DEBUG/secret configuration for every container started from it.
# Runtime values are supplied by Compose; build-time public values are passed as
# build arguments.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

backups
**/*.log

# Host-side development artifacts. These were being copied into the production
# API image by `COPY apps/api/ .`: a 177 MB macOS virtualenv (meaningless, and a
# large attack surface), the test suite, and host-generated `__pycache__`
# bytecode. Stale bytecode whose embedded mtime and size still match the source
# is imported in preference to the .py file, so shipping it risks running code
# that is not the code in the image.
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/*.egg-info
apps/api/tests

# `docs/` is intentionally NOT ignored: the API image reads two reference
# catalogues from it at runtime (see infra/docker/Dockerfile.api).

.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
